IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wk-nouns`

-- Antitrust Guidelines for Business Activities Affecting Workers (2025) -- fixtures shared
-- by the test modules. No rule and no assertion: businesses, pairs of businesses and
-- builders for agreements, exchanges and terms, each named for what it is. Every builder
-- names its fields with WITH; the defaults it fills in are the plain case (employees, no
-- franchise, no platform, no n.15 collaboration, a formal written agreement).

§ `Test fixtures`

§§ `Businesses and pairs`

GIVEN n IS A STRING
      markets IS A LIST OF STRING
      products IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A `Business`
`a business named` MEANS `Business` WITH
    `the name of the business` IS n
    `the labor markets in which it hires or retains workers` IS markets
    `the products or services it makes, sells or provides` IS products

-- Acme and Bolt hire software engineers and sell different things; Cove sells what Acme
-- sells and hires nurses; Quiet names no labor market.
`Acme` MEANS `a business named` "Acme" (LIST "software engineers") (LIST "widgets")
`Bolt` MEANS `a business named` "Bolt" (LIST "software engineers") (LIST "insurance")
`Cove` MEANS `a business named` "Cove" (LIST "nurses") (LIST "widgets")
`Quiet` MEANS `a business named` "Quiet" EMPTY (LIST "widgets")

GIVEN one IS A `Business`
      other IS A `Business`
      potential IS A BOOLEAN
      collaborative IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Two businesses`
`the pair` MEANS `Two businesses` WITH
    `one business` IS one
    `the other business` IS other
    `the businesses are potentially competing employers` IS potential
    `they have some other collaborative or cooperative relationship, such as a joint venture` IS collaborative

`competitors for workers` MEANS `the pair` `Acme` `Bolt` FALSE FALSE
`potentially competing employers` MEANS `the pair` `Acme` `Cove` TRUE FALSE
`businesses that do not compete for workers` MEANS `the pair` `Acme` `Cove` FALSE FALSE
`businesses whose labor markets are not stated` MEANS `the pair` `Acme` `Quiet` FALSE FALSE

-- Two ride platforms through which independent contractors offer their services; both
-- engage app-based drivers (6 [pdf page 11]).
`ride platform A` MEANS `a business named` "ride platform A" (LIST "app-based drivers") (LIST "rides")
`ride platform B` MEANS `a business named` "ride platform B" (LIST "app-based drivers") (LIST "deliveries")
`the competing platforms` MEANS `the pair` `ride platform A` `ride platform B` FALSE FALSE

§§ `Agreements between businesses`

`a formal written agreement` MEANS `Form of the agreement` WITH
    `it is formal` IS TRUE
    `it is express` IS TRUE
    `it is written down` IS TRUE
    `it was spoken or talked about` IS TRUE
    `it was ever carried out` IS TRUE
    `it was made by individuals at the businesses rather than by the businesses themselves` IS FALSE
    `it was entered into through an intermediary` IS FALSE
    `it resulted in actual harm such as lower wages` IS TRUE

-- The general principles' and section 1's other forms, all at once: informal, implicit,
-- unwritten, never talked about, never carried out, made by individuals at the businesses,
-- through an intermediary, and doing no actual harm.
`an informal unwritten unspoken agreement never carried out` MEANS `Form of the agreement` WITH
    `it is formal` IS FALSE
    `it is express` IS FALSE
    `it is written down` IS FALSE
    `it was spoken or talked about` IS FALSE
    `it was ever carried out` IS FALSE
    `it was made by individuals at the businesses rather than by the businesses themselves` IS TRUE
    `it was entered into through an intermediary` IS TRUE
    `it resulted in actual harm such as lower wages` IS FALSE

-- Every field, by name. The builders below fill in the plain case.
GIVEN finding IS A `Finding on whether there is an agreement`
      b IS A `Two businesses`
      a IS A `What the businesses agree`
      applicants IS A BOOLEAN
      workers IS A `Kind of workers concerned`
      platforms IS A BOOLEAN
      franchise IS A `Franchise relationship of the parties`
      organizes IS A BOOLEAN
      subordinate IS A BOOLEAN
      necessary IS A BOOLEAN
      form IS A `Form of the agreement`
GIVETH A `Agreement between businesses relating to workers`
`the agreement in full` MEANS `Agreement between businesses relating to workers` WITH
    `the finding on whether there is an agreement` IS finding
    `the businesses` IS b
    `what the businesses agree` IS a
    `the firms remain allowed to hire workers who apply for a position without first being solicited` IS applicants
    `the workers concerned` IS workers
    `the businesses are platforms through which the independent contractors offer their services` IS platforms
    `the franchise relationship of the parties` IS franchise
    `the franchisor organizes or enforces the agreement` IS organizes
    `the restraint is subordinate and collateral to a broader business collaboration, such as a joint venture` IS subordinate
    `the restraint is reasonably necessary to achieve the procompetitive potential of that collaboration` IS necessary
    `the form of the agreement` IS form

GIVEN finding IS A `Finding on whether there is an agreement`
      b IS A `Two businesses`
      a IS A `What the businesses agree`
GIVETH A `Agreement between businesses relating to workers`
`an agreement with the finding` MEANS `the agreement in full` finding b a FALSE `employees` FALSE `no franchise relationship` FALSE FALSE FALSE `a formal written agreement`

GIVEN b IS A `Two businesses`
      a IS A `What the businesses agree`
GIVETH A `Agreement between businesses relating to workers`
`an identified agreement` MEANS `an agreement with the finding` `the agencies identify an agreement between the businesses` b a

GIVEN b IS A `Two businesses`
      a IS A `What the businesses agree`
      form IS A `Form of the agreement`
GIVETH A `Agreement between businesses relating to workers`
`an identified agreement in the form` MEANS `the agreement in full` `the agencies identify an agreement between the businesses` b a FALSE `employees` FALSE `no franchise relationship` FALSE FALSE FALSE form

GIVEN b IS A `Two businesses`
      a IS A `What the businesses agree`
      subordinate IS A BOOLEAN
      necessary IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Agreement between businesses relating to workers`
`an identified agreement with the n.15 findings` MEANS `the agreement in full` `the agencies identify an agreement between the businesses` b a FALSE `employees` FALSE `no franchise relationship` FALSE subordinate necessary `a formal written agreement`

GIVEN b IS A `Two businesses`
      a IS A `What the businesses agree`
      franchise IS A `Franchise relationship of the parties`
      organizes IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Agreement between businesses relating to workers`
`an identified franchise agreement` MEANS `the agreement in full` `the agencies identify an agreement between the businesses` b a FALSE `employees` FALSE franchise organizes FALSE FALSE `a formal written agreement`

GIVEN b IS A `Two businesses`
      a IS A `What the businesses agree`
      workers IS A `Kind of workers concerned`
      platforms IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Agreement between businesses relating to workers`
`an identified agreement about` MEANS `the agreement in full` `the agencies identify an agreement between the businesses` b a FALSE workers platforms `no franchise relationship` FALSE FALSE FALSE `a formal written agreement`

GIVEN b IS A `Two businesses`
      applicants IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Agreement between businesses relating to workers`
`an identified agreement not to cold call workers` MEANS `the agreement in full` `the agencies identify an agreement between the businesses` b `not to cold call workers` applicants `employees` FALSE `no franchise relationship` FALSE FALSE FALSE `a formal written agreement`

-- Terms, by the names the text gives them.
`wage fixing at a level` MEANS `to fix workers' salaries or other terms of compensation or employment, such as bonuses or benefits, at a specific level or within a range`
`no-hire` MEANS `not to recruit, solicit, hire, or otherwise compete for current, former, or potential workers`

§§ `Information exchanges`

-- Every field, by name.
GIVEN b IS A `Two businesses`
      sensitive IS A BOOLEAN
      route IS A `How the information is shared`
      explicit IS A BOOLEAN
      effect IS A `Finding on the exchange's effect`
      intended IS A BOOLEAN
      recommendations IS A BOOLEAN
      adhere IS A BOOLEAN
      useShared IS A BOOLEAN
      discretion IS A BOOLEAN
      shareWages IS A BOOLEAN
      transaction IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Information exchange`
`the exchange in full` MEANS `Information exchange` WITH
    `the businesses` IS b
    `the information is competitively sensitive information about compensation or other terms or conditions of employment` IS sensitive
    `how the information is shared` IS route
    `the exchange is explicit rather than implied from the conduct of the parties` IS explicit
    `the finding on the exchange's effect` IS effect
    `the effect was intended` IS intended
    `the exchange is used to generate wage or other benefit recommendations` IS recommendations
    `the exchange requires the businesses to strictly adhere to the recommendations` IS adhere
    `the businesses agree to use shared wage recommendations, lists, calculations, or algorithms` IS useShared
    `the participants retain some discretion or cheat on the agreement` IS discretion
    `the businesses agree to share information about wages or other terms of employment` IS shareWages
    `the businesses are parties to a legitimate transaction or a joint venture or other collaborative activity` IS transaction

-- A plain exchange of competitively sensitive information: explicit, no recommendations,
-- no agreement to use or share, no transaction.
GIVEN b IS A `Two businesses`
      route IS A `How the information is shared`
      effect IS A `Finding on the exchange's effect`
GIVETH A `Information exchange`
`a sensitive exchange` MEANS `the exchange in full` b TRUE route TRUE effect FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

§§ `Employment terms`

-- Every field, by name.
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of employment term`
      switching IS A BOOLEAN
      competingBusiness IS A BOOLEAN
      limits IS A BOOLEAN
      prevents IS A BOOLEAN
      usableIn IS A BOOLEAN
      chills IS A BOOLEAN
      impedes IS A BOOLEAN
      indications IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Employment term`
`the term in full` MEANS `Employment term` WITH
    `the kind of term` IS kind
    `it restricts the worker from switching jobs` IS switching
    `it restricts the worker from starting a competing business` IS competingBusiness
    `it limits competition` IS limits
    `it functions to prevent the worker from seeking, accepting or working in another job, or from starting a business` IS prevents
    `it prohibits disclosure of any information that is usable in or relates to an industry` IS usableIn
    `it is worded so broadly as to suggest that workers who report potential violations of law, or who cooperate with a government investigation, could face lawsuits and adverse employment consequences` IS chills
    `it impedes worker mobility or otherwise undermines competition` IS impedes
    `there are indications that it is harming competition` IS indications

-- A term of the kind with no finding made.
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of employment term`
GIVETH A `Employment term`
`a bare term` MEANS `the term in full` kind FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- A section 5 term that functions to prevent the worker from taking other work or
-- starting a business, and nothing else found.
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of employment term`
GIVETH A `Employment term`
`a term that prevents leaving` MEANS `the term in full` kind FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

§§ `Earnings claims`

GIVEN isFalse IS A BOOLEAN
      misleading IS A BOOLEAN
      workers IS A `Kind of workers concerned`
GIVETH A `Claim about workers' potential earnings`
`an earnings claim` MEANS `Claim about workers' potential earnings` WITH
    `the claim is false` IS isFalse
    `the claim is misleading` IS misleading
    `the workers concerned` IS workers
